{
  "kanji": "古",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 古\ntitle: old\njlpt: 4\ntags: [jlpt-n4, grade-2, compound, starter]\nstrokes: 5\nradical: 口\nradicalNumber: 30\nonyomi: [コ]\nkunyomi: [ふる.い, ふる-, -ふる.す]\ndistractors: [新, 右, 口]\n---\n\n# 古 — old\n\n**Strokes:** 5 · **Key (radical):** 口 (no. 30) · **JLPT:** N4 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n古 is 十 over 口. A frequently told explanation is \"what has been passed down by mouth through ten generations\", hence \"old, ancient\". This is a mnemonic;\nthe earliest form is debated, and some scholars read the character differently (as a phonetic compound).\n古 means \"old\" for things and times past, not for a person's age.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| コ | on | [中古](../words/中古.md) ちゅうこ (second-hand), 古代 こだい (ancient times), 考古学 こうこがく (archaeology) |\n| ふる.い | kun | [古い](../words/古い.md) ふるい (old; adjective), 古本 ふるほん |\n| ふる- | kun | 古本 ふるほん (secondhand book), 古道具 ふるどうぐ |\n| -ふる.す | kun | 使い古す つかいふるす (wear out through use) |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [古い](../words/古い.md) ふるい — old\n- [中古](../words/中古.md) ちゅうこ — second-hand, used\n- 古本 ふるほん — second-hand book\n- [古典](../words/古典.md) こてん — classic work; the classics\n\n## Notes\n\nIts opposite is [新](新.md). 古い is for things and ideas; for a person's age use 年を取った としをとった or 年寄り としより (elderly person); 年上 としうえ means \"older than me\".\nLook-alikes: 右 ([右](右.md)), which has a diagonal stroke instead of the vertical; 石 (stone), which has 厂 on top; 苦 (bitter), which has 艹 on top.\n",
